Deployment: SDD

Purpose:
  Define deployment strategies, environment management, and release
  management principles. Strategy selection depends on risk tolerance,
  team maturity, and project scale.

Principles:
  Every deploy MUST be reversible.
  Deployments MUST be automated.
  Environments MUST mirror production as closely as possible.
  Rollback MUST be faster than forward fix.
  Deployments MUST be tested before production.

Strategies:

  BlueGreen:
    description: Two identical environments, switch traffic atomically
    process: deploy to idle environment, run smoke tests, switch traffic
    benefits: instant rollback, zero downtime
    costs: double infrastructure, database migration complexity
    when_to_use: L2-L5, low downtime tolerance

  Canary:
    description: Gradually route traffic to new version
    process: deploy alongside old, route 1-5% to new, monitor, gradually increase or rollback
    benefits: early issue detection, limited blast radius
    costs: requires traffic splitting, robust monitoring
    when_to_use: L3-L5, high traffic, strong observability

  Rolling:
    description: Replace instances one by one
    process: take instance out of rotation, deploy, verify health, next
    benefits: no double infrastructure, gradual rollout
    costs: mixed versions during deployment
    when_to_use: L2-L4, stateless, backward-compatible, constrained budget

  Immutable:
    description: Replace entire infrastructure on each deploy
    process: build new image, deploy new instances, terminate old
    benefits: known state, no configuration drift, instant rollback
    costs: requires container orchestration
    when_to_use: L3-L5, containerized, strong CI/CD maturity

Environments:
  required:
    development: local environments, shared DB, mock services
    staging: mirrors production, anonymized data, PR merge deploy
    production: real traffic, real data, highest availability
  optional:
    testing: automated tests, ephemeral
    preview: per-PR deploy, manual QA
  rule: staging MUST mirror production configuration

CI_CD:
  pipeline: source -> build -> test -> staging -> production
  rules:
    every_commit_triggers: pipeline MUST complete before merge
    fail_fast: pipeline MUST fail on first stage failure
    artifact_immutability: same artifact deploys to all environments
    secrets: MUST NOT be in source code, injected at deploy time

ReleaseManagement:
  versioning: semantic versioning (major.minor.patch)
  change_management:
    standard_change: routine deploy, pre-approved, automated
    normal_change: new feature, requires review, scheduled window
    emergency_change: critical fix, expedited approval, post-deploy review
  rollback: target MUST be defined before deploy, procedure MUST be tested

Selection:
  strategy_selection:
    low_risk_frequent: canary or rolling (L3-L5)
    high_risk_infrequent: blue-green or immutable (L2-L4)
    constrained_infrastructure: rolling (L2-L3)

AntiPatterns:
  DeployOnFriday: critical deploys MUST have monitoring coverage
  ManualDeploy: every deployment MUST be automated
  DeployToProductionFirst: MUST test in staging before production
  NoRollbackPlan: rollback plan MUST exist and be tested
  ConfigurationDrift: infrastructure MUST be immutable and code-defined
  BigBangDeploy: deploy small, frequent changes
  NoMonitoring: deploy MUST include monitoring and alerting

Navigation:
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd
  Availability: @availability.sdd

State: +